############################################################
Cart command limits: +/-12.0 m/s^2, +/-0.80 m/s
Ramp position limit: +/-300 mm from z
Enter one command per line: z=zero DD at centre; q/w/e/r=UU/UD/DU/DD; p=start selected hold (q/w/e).
rw=DD->UD; re=DD->DU; rq=DD->UU; x=OFF. Each start keeps the cart origin from z.
During a hold: e = UD->DU or UU->DU; w = DU->UD or UU->UD; q = DU->UU or UD->UU. Each starts once the hold has been
still and centred for 1 s (gives up after 10 s).
x during a UU/UD/DU hold = soft stop: descend to DD, damp, then OFF. x again (or x in a swing) = OFF now.
r during a UU/UD/DU hold = descend to DD and wait with the motor on; then q/w/e swings up again.
z saves DD angles and cart ramp origin; h reads encoder counters; lc clears RE learning. Motor OFF commands.
